Track 2: Photoperiod Clipping
- Story & Context: Hidden away in the humid rot of the mall's sunken interior greenhouse, Declan Moss spent two straight days nursing blistering chemical burns on his fingers after siphoning leaded gasoline to keep the arcade's backup generators running. He had pushed their voltage transformers past safety limits to saturate Vance’s bowed double bass drones in infinite, starry reverb trails, only for a high-pressure sodium grow lamp to explode overhead and shower the mixing board in molten yellow glass. Still bleeding onto the faders while Rook tracked her most desperate, fuzz-shredded guitar take of the winter, Declan leaned into the intercom to utter the exhausted confession that anchored the chorus: "we grow best under artificial scald."
