Track 3: Galleria Terrarium No. 4
- Story & Context: By the sub-zero morning the county demolition bulldozers finally encircled Galleria Terrarium No. 4, the abandoned atrium had already hardened into local urban folklore. Nearly two hundred shivering kids had barricaded the heavy iron roll-down security shutters with broken vending machines, screaming the lyrics as Vance's double bass vibrated so violently it shook sheets of dead moss from the ceiling girders onto the dancing crowd. When the police cutting torches finally punched through the locks at dawn, they found only warm amplifier tubes, piles of severed arcade wiring, and Rook’s defiant final statement spray-painted across the concrete planter: "nothing dies beneath a shattered glass roof."
